<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:56:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Democrat Hubbard wins North Carolina recount, clinching historic House majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93e11207c77bacb58e323998add3beffe9c71eee7d151fe9a1becd5ed8ee1c2d</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:56:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T20:16:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261122-democrat-hubbard-wins-north-carolina-recount-clinching-historic-house-majority--58e941bd0d61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261122-democrat-hubbard-wins-north-carolina-recount-clinching-historic-house-majority" /><summary type="html">Democrat Chuck Hubbard was elected to the US House of Representatives from North Carolina on Sunday after defeating veteran Republican Virginia Foxx, who chairs the powerful House Rules Committee. His victory gave Democrats their best general election result in decades, winning at least 258 seats in the 2026 US midterms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>FBI criminal database hacked</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:543247ea107e5aebadb4b64a91df3d382af7410ac970920343e58c3b371104a7</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T17:23:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/fbi-criminal-database-hacked--0e998fd7b8f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fbi-criminal-database-hacked" /><summary type="html">The FBI is investigating a reported major cyberattack targeting its national law enforcement database, the National Crime Information Center (NCIC), which holds sensitive criminal justice records, including information on fugitives, missing persons, criminal histories and stolen property. President Donald Trump said he had just been briefed on the incident, describing it as “not good”. FRANCE 24’s Fraser Jackson reports from Washington DC.</summary></entry><entry><title>Man convicted of starting palisades fire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f264c4544ade5ad44b66258df41dd0f5c67ae6bfe17351646cf681d09f56df0</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T17:21:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/man-convicted-of-starting-palisades-fire--96bd39830bc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/man-convicted-of-starting-palisades-fire" /><summary type="html">A Los Angeles County jury found former rideshare driver Jonathan Rinderknecht guilty on Friday of starting the 2025 Palisades fire, which caused widespread destruction and loss of life. He faces a prison sentence of between five and 40 years. Liza Kaminov has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mexico captures drug cartel boss ‘El Chapo Isidro’ after deadly firefight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29eb6231c036d8462750f6cddb51c064b6fcf033b946871e0509d9fed5841546</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T15:00:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-mexico-captures-drug-cartel-boss-el-chapo-isidro-after-deadly-firefight--4de2de04ed1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-mexico-captures-drug-cartel-boss-el-chapo-isidro-after-deadly-firefight" /><summary type="html">Mexico's military forces captured ​one of the most wanted suspected drug lords, Fausto Isidro Meza Flores, known as "El Chapo Isidro," the military announced on Saturday, after a deadly firefight that killed seven suspected attackers and four soldiers. Flores, one of the FBI’s 10 most wanted fugitives, was flown to Mexico City after his capture.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Agriculture Department and FBI hit by cyberattacks, media report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b8ab1c85a636c8f25aaa4f71932e61e4cc5cd47974deb51d71311025b291c14</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T07:01:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-us-agriculture-department-fbi-hit-by-cyberattacks-media-report--56cdf33f7140.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-us-agriculture-department-fbi-hit-by-cyberattacks-media-report" /><summary type="html">Hackers breached systerms at the US Agriculture Department and the FBI, US media reported, amid a recent wave of major technology disruptions across the country.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>House of Cards: America's enemies "no longer fear it, its allies no longer trust it'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98723359d18259a91efae087fd1633306e55375044a0c6b766e011e2790c3220</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T22:13:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-house-of-cards-america-s-enemies-no-longer-fear-it-its-allies-no-longer-trust-it--88bb89bac749.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-house-of-cards-america-s-enemies-no-longer-fear-it-its-allies-no-longer-trust-it" /><summary type="html">The Economist's deputy editor Tom Standage joins us for a futuristic retrospective, taking us back to the future as we spotlight "The World Ahead 2027". We begin with the "leader of the free world", the FIFA Peace Prize recipient presiding over an America under the "Donroe Doctrine": "Its enemies no longer fear it and its allies no longer trust it in the way they did before."</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>🦛 USA: Fiona, Cincinnati Zoo’s famous hippo, has died</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ea0e5d5c61b06e2af24159d41f6b887bd2c9b1ab6142e69b8101a904cd2f4c8</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T17:35:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-_-usa-fiona-cincinnati-zoo-s-famous-hippo-has-died--6b77bb696bc5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-%F0%9F%A6%9B-usa-fiona-cincinnati-zoo-s-famous-hippo-has-died" /><summary type="html">🦛Fiona, Cincinnati Zoo’s beloved hippo, has died aged just 9, after swallowing a knitted hat that fell into her enclosure. Born prematurely and weighing only 13kg, she captured millions of hearts around the world and became an internet sensation.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump hails 'fantastic' relationships with China's Xi, Russia's Putin after three-way talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f09b6e0d252c69af3b24011c853ac1edf2dd87b70075af44e5a11adefc802070</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T16:30:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-watch-live-trump-holds-press-conference-meeting-xi-putin--de6586fb5a55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-watch-live-trump-holds-press-conference-meeting-xi-putin" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump played up his "fantastic" relationships with China's Xi Jinping and Russia's Vladimir Putin during a White House press conference on Friday following his return to Washington after a first-ever trilateral meeting with the Chinese and Russian leaders. Here are key takeaways from his wide-ranging briefing.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Jamaica's beaches are increasingly off limits to locals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e64873b27d588c9db584014178c65f6224baba3b94329665678cfa0b7c14f2b</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:55:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261120-jamaica-beaches-off-limits-to-locals-property-developers-hotels--8b1ba04df6ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261120-jamaica-beaches-off-limits-to-locals-property-developers-hotels" /><summary type="html">Jamaica usually conjures up images of white sandy beaches, Rastafari culture and Bob Marley – but another reality exists. On this small Caribbean island, less than 1 percent of the coastline is freely accessible to local people. The rest has gradually been privatised, mostly for large hotel developments and private homes.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>El Salvador: Nayib Bukele, self-proclaimed “coolest dictator on earth”, is seeking a third term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7dc638fc57c038a932d573cee526a669f6b74fc90629e8dbdd625340b5bb019c</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:07:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-self-proclaimed-coolest-dictator-on-earth-is-seeking-a-third-term--1aebd0b55990.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-self-proclaimed-coolest-dictator-on-earth-is-seeking-a-third-term" /><summary type="html">🇸🇻 El Salvador’s President Nayib Bukele, who calls himself the “coolest dictator on earth”, is seeking a third term after changing the Constitution to scrap presidential term limits. His war on gangs has made him hugely popular, but also sparked serious human rights concerns.</summary></entry><entry><title>White House fires national cyber director over widespread outages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6387e2e253960dbd4c5dd2cb01a331d7d8981111a4fd18502e429984a9bc9c93</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T01:28:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-white-house-fires-national-cyber-director-over-widespread-outages--e5d5af4d4476.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-white-house-fires-national-cyber-director-over-widespread-outages" /><summary type="html">The White House fired national cyber director Sean Cairncross on Thursday following a week of technology disruptions affecting US air travel, email services and national security systems. The departure comes as the Trump administration faces criticism over its response to the outages, which officials say were unrelated incidents.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Armed forces in Haiti kill at least 34 gang members to regain control of key corridor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed7d7a37da62a920f87904d7a0b4abfa7193fada934a4fbbf92b9a22902b2e8d</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T22:31:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261119-major-anti-gang-offensive-in-haiti-kills-34-suspected-gang-members--26a4355e6e18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261119-major-anti-gang-offensive-in-haiti-kills-34-suspected-gang-members" /><summary type="html">Haitian security forces launched a major offensive on Thursday to retake Martissant, a strategic corridor linking Port-au-Prince with the country's western and southern regions that gangs have controlled for five years. Police said at least 34 suspected gang members were killed in clashes involving a private security task force.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>A president among body bags: Photo ops spark outrage in Colombia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19dc3c09d9d7a6ba32dd635620726ee6c8e69c71ed21c80c00c27055c9e378c2</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:52:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261119-president-body-bags-photo-ops-sparking-outrage-colombia--7fdcc25cb912.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261119-president-body-bags-photo-ops-sparking-outrage-colombia" /><summary type="html">Since taking office in August, Colombia's far-right President Abelardo de la Espriella has regularly posted videos that show him walking among body bags supposedly holding the remains of rebel fighters – a communications strategy that has sparked widespread criticism.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>NASA's Voyager 1 phones home from record one light-day away, 49 years after launch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:714cd6db5955704531a871897790fa9989fc5f510fe813f4c3714829be54f8d0</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:26:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nasa-voyager-1-phones-home-from-record-one-light-day-away-49-years-after-launch--ea85baca7960.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nasa-voyager-1-phones-home-from-record-one-light-day-away-49-years-after-launch" /><summary type="html">The Voyager 1 probe launched by NASA nearly a half century ago has reached a distance from Earth of one light day (more than 26 billion kilometres), the farthest any human artifact has ever ventured from our planet. The space agency received a signal from the spacecraft Thursday, exactly 24 hours after it was sent.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Xi, Putin summit: What was it all about?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38bf090f5361b3291ff4e8ed32ce51ec6f29f612e5469c6e06a6522c5877f8be</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:12:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-xi-putin-summit-what-was-it-all-about--2c0baba62b07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-xi-putin-summit-what-was-it-all-about" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has left China after a historic first meeting with Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the APEC summit. Ukraine was discussed without Kyiv or European leaders in the room, which raised eyebrows, though Trump defended dialogue with rivals and Putin said the talks created conditions for future agreements. Xi warned major powers against conflict, and topics included reducing nuclear risks, reforming the UN and increasing energy flows.</summary></entry><entry><title>Haiti: Salvador’s Bukele publishes video of attack on gang leader’s house</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ed2dd89f51c21b51eb153a60ec558a603cc17d5be93c587f509217175afb0d4</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:06:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-haiti-salvador-s-bukele-publishes-video-of-attack-on-gang-leader-s-house--14ac3f8f83f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-haiti-salvador-s-bukele-publishes-video-of-attack-on-gang-leader-s-house" /><summary type="html">Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele said Wednesday that his troops demolished the lavish home of a prominent gang leader in Haiti known as Jeff Gwo Lwa. "My gift to the Haitian people on the anniversary of the Battle of Vertières," Bukele wrote on X - referencing a 1803 battle critical in helping secure Haiti's independence from France.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Democrats nominate Jeffries to be first Black House speaker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9b59ea08d0428d33184f4df9c6982d85682c373a63a4015511f536656511b50</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:58:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-democrats-nominate-jeffries-to-be-first-black-house-speaker--1a82a2206b26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-democrats-nominate-jeffries-to-be-first-black-house-speaker" /><summary type="html">Hakeem Jeffries is on the cusp of becoming the first Black speaker of the US House of Representatives after Democrats elected him their leader Wednesday following a sweeping midterm election triumph. Jeffries faced no declared challenger, although opposition from some newly elected progressives had exposed divisions over how Democrats should wield their newfound power. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hegseth makes surprise trip to Venezuela, renews military cooperation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f569e4f888c51128fc638652113c2a513fe75090d0713cb84773345dcce0dd8</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T18:59:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-hegseth-makes-surprise-trip-to-venezuela-renews-military-cooperation--c69718d51c80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-hegseth-makes-surprise-trip-to-venezuela-renews-military-cooperation" /><summary type="html">US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth made an unannounced visit to Caracas on Wednesday, announcing a resumption of military cooperation with Venezuela and vowing to crack down on drug traffickers. The trip marks the highest-level US visit since the ouster of Nicolas Maduro in January, signalling a dramatic shift in relations between the two countries.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Beijing has supported Moscow but 'China understands that America is way more important than Russia'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a519af091d54a71d0c572e4be7115b931d4c4adcb8df358d076047d087dab324</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T17:48:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia--f9f88efc8e97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia" /><summary type="html">Following Xi Jinping's very friendly rare tarmac greeting for Donald Trump, Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Kerry Brown, Professor of Chinese Studies and Director of the Lau China Institute at King's College, London. Brown examines the complex relationship between the world's two largest economies, China's growing diplomatic influence and the competition over artificial intelligence.“China is the diplomatic center of the world,” says Brown, pointing to Beijing's ability to bring together leaders from Russia, the United States, Europe and elsewhere. He argues that China now has “extraordinary convening power" and significant influence over Russia.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Democrats nominate Hakeem Jeffries to be first Black speaker of the House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e5a98dfd003f4ff8091f890f16f87e17a9441a0b2205523b9f8d82e4b1579c5</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:44:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-us-democrats-nominate-hakeem-jeffries-to-be-first-black-speaker-of-the-house--380c6ed3ece3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-us-democrats-nominate-hakeem-jeffries-to-be-first-black-speaker-of-the-house" /><summary type="html">Democrats nominated Hakeem Jeffries on Wednesday to be the next speaker of the House of Representatives, putting him on track to make history as the nation’s first Black American with the gavel.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Peltola defeats Sullivan in Alaska Senate race, expanding Democratic majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecf636887c0f5e76289aea59380fce64ab6913e47d9e91c28288086393ea1ddf</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T03:47:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-peltola-defeats-sullivan-in-alaska-senate-race-expanding-democratic-majority--a4d690c354ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-peltola-defeats-sullivan-in-alaska-senate-race-expanding-democratic-majority" /><summary type="html">Democrat Mary Peltola defeated Republican Sen. Dan Sullivan in Alaska on Tuesday, completing a political comeback in a state that US President Donald Trump has repeatedly won by wide margins. Her victory gives Democrats a 56-44 Senate majority, marking their biggest net gain in Senate seats since 1958.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Haitians rally behind Bukele as Salvadoran troops battle gangs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bef17d4bb5a7a912e7fb2d123755bdbd36774ae0da44d6737ddeedace39312c7</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T02:42:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-haitians-rally-behind-bukele-as-salvadoran-troops-battle-gangs--576572e0300d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-haitians-rally-behind-bukele-as-salvadoran-troops-battle-gangs" /><summary type="html">Thousands of Haitians took to the streets on Tuesday to urge El Salvador's President Nayib Bukele to keep fighting gangs, as his troops bolster security forces in the Caribbean nation. But experts warn that growing public support could turn to anger without a long-term plan to tackle violence and strengthen Haiti's police.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US, Mexico and Bolivia lose measles-free status as deaths mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a3c4ad7aff6e39376edd37b4e29607a9a275e64225dc359c416f733fe6e0c56</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T21:30:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-us-mexico-and-bolivia-lose-measles-free-status-as-deaths-mount--3ecebbb665bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-us-mexico-and-bolivia-lose-measles-free-status-as-deaths-mount" /><summary type="html">The US has lost its measles-free status, international health officials said Tuesday, as the highly contagious virus has spread at the fastest rate in more than 30 years, while Mexico and Bolivia also lost their measles-elimination status. Vaccination rates have been falling against a number of diseases, in the US and globally, and measles has been spreading throughout the Americas since 2024.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Iran 'playing mind games with the United States', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:490c4cd3de511871dafe06e8fc73d1289f3a75f23a583de12a0c2e113ab6aab8</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T20:28:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-playing-mind-games-with-the-united-states-expert-says--5ddc4f0f722f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-playing-mind-games-with-the-united-states-expert-says" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump said Tuesday that US authorities take "very seriously" any possible threat to Washington, following reports Iran was planning to target officials, possibly with a radioactive bomb. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Stimson Center in Washington, says that Iran may be "playing mind games with the United States as a way perhaps of deterring President Trump from unleashing a massive new attack on Iran".</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says he takes possible Iran bomb threat to Washington 'very seriously'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3cc3cd246af440e0d9bf67b9fa687cdad4b6c127247b60a93925c841fa36d51</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T15:44:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-trump-says-he-takes-possible-iran-bomb-threat-to-washington-very-seriously--b7da002abc8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-trump-says-he-takes-possible-iran-bomb-threat-to-washington-very-seriously" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump said Tuesday that US authorities take any possible threats to Washington ‘very seriously’, following reports that Iran was planning to target senior Trump administration officials, possibly with a radioactive bomb.  Tehran dismissed the reports as ‘fabricated’.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Chase outage disrupts US online banking, Zelle payments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c17cd578c5378be69ac433dfd0f8d5e92b308d1867eb06c06f5f9f2b3da12483</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:40:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-chase-outage-disrupts-online-banking-and-zelle-payments-in-united-states-us-software--69cbbbd1d139.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-chase-outage-disrupts-online-banking-and-zelle-payments-in-united-states-us-software" /><summary type="html">Users of several major US banking apps and online portals reported outages on Monday, according to the monitoring site Downdetector.com, with one institution ruling out a cyberattack as the cause. Among those affected by the outages were Bank of America, JPMorgan Chase and the popular money transfer app Zelle.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says he needs funding for air traffic control after ground stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a8481a74613af8998a26ace91a20ef874ba5d957686b5913ce081dd4d4f891f</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:01:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-says-he-needs-funding-for-air-traffic-control-after-ground-stop--48f92ae1d591.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-says-he-needs-funding-for-air-traffic-control-after-ground-stop" /><summary type="html">US ​President ​Donald Trump, pressed on a ​technology ‌failure ⁠that ‌grounded thousands of ⁠flights last week, ​on ‌Monday told reporters ‌that ​the government needed funding for upgrade ​to ​air traffic ​control equipment. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Sheldon Jacobson, Professor of Computer Science at the University of Illinois. He explains that "the Republicans have had full control of the House and the Senate since the President came in. They controlled everything. If they needed the money and wanted the money they could have approved the money. The fact that they didn't, in the the different bills that have been passed, suggests that it's more than just money that is going on here".</summary></entry><entry><title>US judge strikes down Trump visa restrictions on foreign students, journalists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fe006c47f251dc60be90c2848887d4baa1f780d87f7cf22a6c1b03ef419677b</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T21:23:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-us-judge-strikes-down-trump-visa-restrictions-on-foreign-students-journalists--89359086d5e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-us-judge-strikes-down-trump-visa-restrictions-on-foreign-students-journalists" /><summary type="html">A US federal judge struck down a Trump administration policy on Monday that would have sharply limited the length of time foreign students and journalists could stay in the country, ruling that the proposed restrictions were unlawful and would undermine educational opportunity.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>November 17 blackout hoax: How a conspiracy theory went viral around the world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0a3644e8c2b579a591df639c47a5a98b80aedefa0ce138284c7471999ec2835</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:50:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261116-november-17-blackout-hoax-how-a-conspiracy-theory-went-viral-around-the-world--0b2ddebc84cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261116-november-17-blackout-hoax-how-a-conspiracy-theory-went-viral-around-the-world" /><summary type="html">A conspiracy theory claiming a worldwide "blackout" will hit the world on November 17 has spread across social media, with the claim it will cut electricity, internet and banking services. The rumour stems from a routine US FEMA emergency alert test, but was amplified by cryptocurrency accounts, misleading claims about EU preparedness advice and references to "The Simpsons". Recent technology outages, flight disruptions and cyberattacks have added to public anxiety, helping turn a routine test into a global hoax.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Pope concludes South America homecoming, reassures faithful after cancer scare</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18622000feac15032e3d84c9bae081dd11f2f684d8a80f8bfb2bb1359461c3ad</id><updated>2026-11-22T21:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:50:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-pope-concludes-south-america-homecoming-reassures-faithful-after-cancer-scare--0f38c5877379.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-pope-concludes-south-america-homecoming-reassures-faithful-after-cancer-scare" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV finished Monday his 12-day tour of Uruguay, Argentina and Peru reiterating his advocacy for social justice, environmental protection and the importance of community. Just a month after undergoing lung cancer surgery, the 71-year-old pontiff drew millions of faithful across South America, where he spent nearly two decades as a missionary.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
